    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nWhen building cython 3.3.1, there is non-deterministic code generation.  Specifically, `Cython/Compiler/Parsing.c` sometimes has the following code but not always:\n\n```\n__pyx_v_6Cython_8Compiler_7Parsing__unicode·=·Py_None;·Py_INCREF(Py_None);\n__pyx_v_6Cython_8Compiler_7Parsing__bytes·=·Py_None;·Py_INCREF(Py_None);\n__pyx_v_6Cython_8Compiler_7Parsing__parse_escape_sequences·=·Py_None;·Py_INCREF(Py_None);\n__pyx_v_6Cython_8Compiler_7Parsing__parse_escape_sequences_raw·=·Py_None;·Py_INCREF(Py_None);\n```\n\nA side-by-side comparison of the compiled code (that gets packaged up, thus it's in distro packages in this report) can be seen at https://valkyrie.yocto.io/pub/repro-fail/oe-reproducible-20261111-opb4ps2w/packages/diff-html/#reproducibleA-tmp---reproducibleA-tmp-deploy---reproducibleA-tmp-deploy-ipk---reproducibleA-tmp-deploy-ipk-x------v----reproducibleA-tmp-deploy-ipk-x------v--python--cython-src_-.-.--r-_x------v-.ipk---data.tar.zst---data.tar---.-usr-src-debug-python--cython--.-.--Cython-Compiler-Parsing.c.\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\n_No response_\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\n_No response_\n\n### OS\n\nLinux\n\n### Python version\n\n3.14.10\n\n### Cython version\n\n3.3.1\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "None of the declarations that lead to those variables look used to me. So superficially we could just delete them. But it'd still be good to understand why it isn't reproducible.\n\nAre you building with any kind of parallelism?\n\nMy guess would be it's just a different version of the `cimport_from_pyx` parallel issue that wasn't fixed in this release. (i.e. it's possibly just the \"unused\" detection behaving differently with/without `cimport_from_pyx`). But that is just a guess.",
